    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Oldtown is a beautifully located, spacious residence set on a quiet rural road leading directly to the beach, practically adjacent to one of the most stunning stretches of the South East coastline at Tomhaggard. Ballyhealy Beach is just around the corner, offering miles of golden sand, while The White Hole — only two minutes away — provides a superb wildlife haven connected to  Tacumshane Lakes, renowned for birdlife and natural beauty. The surrounding countryside offers magnificent walks, peaceful scenery, and an exceptional outdoor lifestyle. A short drive brings you to Kilmore Quay, which has recently undergone a complete infrastructural upgrade, now featuring an attractive modern marina, excellent seafood restaurants, and daily boat trips to the Saltee Islands. Everyday amenities including shops, schools, churches, and even third level facilities in Bridgetown are all within easy reach. The property enjoys excellent regional connectivity: approximately 25 minutes to Wexford Town, a short distance to Rosslare Europort for ferry travel, 1 hour to Waterford City/Airport, and 2 hours to Dublin City/Airport. Set on a generous site, the home is approached by a tarmac driveway that wraps fully around the house, providing superb circulation and ample parking. The front and rear gardens are well maintained and offer excellent\r\noutdoor space. Inside, the residence is presented in excellent condition throughout, offering bright, spacious and practical accommodation ideal as a family home or holiday retreat. A spacious entrance hallway leads to both the lounge and living room, each fitted with its own stove, creating warm, inviting spaces. The kitchen/dining area is well proportioned, supported by a utility room off and a convenient WC. Upstairs, there are four double bedrooms. One features an ensuite and walk in wardrobe, while two others include built in wardrobes, providing excellent storage. The home benefits from double glazed windows, strong insulation, excellent gardens, ample parking, and quality broadband. A detached garage completes the property, ideal for storage, workshop use, or hobby space. This is a rare opportunity to acquire a beautifully located coastal residence with superb amenities, exceptional natural surroundings, and outstanding connectivity. Viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation Comprises:\r\nEntrance Hallway – (3.85m x 3.64m),  Solid Ash floor, natural timber staircase to first floor, wall lights, phone point.\r\nLounge – (4.71m x 4.00m),  Carpeted, stove with marble surround, coving and centre rose.\r\nLiving Room – (6.74m x 3.9),  Semi solid wooden floor, Bay window, TV & phone points, French doors to side of property, stove with wooden surround, wall lights, coving and centre rose.\r\nKitchen/Dining Area – (5.44m x 4.47m),  Tiled floor, Bay window, Pitch pine eye & waist level kitchen units, oven, 5 ring gas hob and ext. fan, tiled splashback, coving.\r\nUtility Room – (3.50m x 2.34m),  Tiled floor, door to back of property, plumbed for washing machine storage cupboards, hotpress off, wc, off.\r\nWC – (2.17m x 1.17m),  Tiled floor, wc & whb.\r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\n\r\nLanding – (4.99m x 3.64m),  Varnished timber floor, coving and centre rose.\r\nMaster Bedroom – (4.71m x 3.53m),  Varnished timber floor. Walk in wardrobe off shelved and railed, access to attic.\r\nEn-Suite – (2.53m x 1.77m),  Tiled floor and half way up walls, wc, whb, Triton corner shower fully tiled.\r\nBedroom No. 2 – (3.92m x 3.09m),  Varnished timber floor, Built in wardrobes, TVpoint.\r\nBedroom No. 3 – (4.72m x 3.01m),  Varnished timber floor, built in wardrobes & chest of drawers.\r\nBathroom – (3.62m x 2.16m),  Tiled floor and half way up walls, corner bath, wc & whb, Triton shower.\r\nBedroom No. 4 – (3.93m x 2.75m),  Carpeted, TV point.\r\n\r\nDetached Garage 6.78m x 3.71m Roller door to the front, door to side.\r\n\r\nOutside: Gated entrance, tarmacadamed drive, gardens to front, rear & side, drive around facility, spacious parking, detached garage.\r\nServices: Electricity, mains water, private sewerage, oil fired central heating.\r\nBER: B Ber No: 119766673 Performance indicator: 137.5 Wh/m2/yr\r\nApply: Keane Auctioneers (053) 9123072"
